    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">In the other programs.</text:span><text:s/>In the browser, <text:span text:style-name="T1">F1</text:span><text:s/>lists the shortcuts. In the terminal, <text:span text:style-name="T2">]</text:span><text:s/>and <text:span text:style-name="T2">[</text:span><text:s/>go to the next and previous misspelt word, <text:span text:style-name="T2">}</text:span><text:s/>and <text:span text:style-name="T2">{</text:span><text:s/>to the next and previous grammar finding. On Windows, <text:span text:style-name="T1">F7</text:span><text:s/>goes to the next misspelt word and <text:span text:style-name="T1">Ctrl+F7</text:span><text:s/>to the next grammar finding; on the Mac, <text:span text:style-name="T1">Option+Cmd+;</text:span><text:s/>goes to the next grammar finding.</text:p>
    <text:h text:outline-level="1">Appendix B: Glossary</text:h>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Block.</text:span><text:s/>A paragraph, heading or list item in a text document.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Bookmark.</text:span><text:s/>A name for a place in a text document, which keeps pointing at the same place when you edit above it.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Cell.</text:span><text:s/>One box of a spreadsheet, named by its column and row, such as B3.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Command palette.</text:span><text:s/>The searchable list of every command, opened with Ctrl+K.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Flat file.</text:span><text:s/>An ODF document saved as one plain text file: <text:span text:style-name="T2">.fods</text:span><text:s/>or <text:span text:style-name="T2">.fodt</text:span>.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Formula.</text:span><text:s/>A cell entry that starts with <text:span text:style-name="T2">=</text:span><text:s/>and calculates a value.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Lint.</text:span><text:s/>An automatic check of a document for mistakes.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Locale.</text:span><text:s/>The conventions a document follows for writing numbers, such as which character is the decimal point.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">ODF.</text:span><text:s/>The OpenDocument Format, the open standard grind uses for its files.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Package.</text:span><text:s/>An ODF document saved as a compressed archive: <text:span text:style-name="T2">.ods</text:span><text:s/>or <text:span text:style-name="T2">.odt</text:span>.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Range.</text:span><text:s/>A rectangle of cells, named by two corners, such as B2:B7.</text:p>
    <text:p><text:span text:style-name="T1">Template.</text:span><text:s/>A document that provides the page, the letterhead and the styles for other documents.</text:p>
  </office:text>
 </office:body>
</office:document>
